   "spoken": "The lesson Black ignored: he pushed pawns without controlling the center, so we got a free hand. The right plan against his e5 wall is to reroute the knight to d2, push f4-f5, and take on e6 — because the f-file leads straight at the king, and once it opens mate can follow in a couple of moves.",
